    if (n <= 1) return 1;
    return n * factorial(n - 1);
}

output:
int factorial(int n) {
    int res = 1;
    for (int i = 2; i <= n; ++i) res *= i;
    return res;
}
---
Converted recursion to iteration. Deep recursion consumes stack space and involves function call overhead (push/pop registers). The iterative solution uses constant O(1) memory and is faster for the CPU.

